 The admin Website setting can hide Galleries from navigation once every listed public gallery is changed to Unlisted, taken offline, or changed to password-protected access. Unlisted public galleries stay accessible without a password by direct link and do not block the setting. Public drafts and offline galleries do not block it either; they may only be republished as Unlisted while it stays hidden. The Home recent-gallery and showcase sections, public gallery directory API, and `/galleries` page stop promoting galleries; the portfolio remains visible. Direct `/e/*` customer links retain their existing availability and password rules. New galleries start protected. The admin always shows a copyable direct URL for each gallery, including drafts and offline galleries; a copied link only works when the gallery is available. This switch does not delete media or revoke a protected-gallery grant.
 
-The Worker serves `/robots.txt` as text and `/sitemap.xml` as XML on every site profile. The sitemap contains paired `/fr/` and `/en/` marketing pages and published `/fr/portfolio/:slug` and `/en/portfolio/:slug` collections with reciprocal `hreflang`; `/galleries` and every `/e/*` customer gallery URL are omitted regardless of status. Both paths stay in `assets.run_worker_first` so the SPA fallback cannot replace them with HTML. The customer gallery directory and pages use `noindex,nofollow`; public gallery direct links still provide social preview metadata. A D1 outage leaves the static marketing sitemap available without collection URLs.
+The Worker serves `/robots.txt` as text and `/sitemap.xml` as XML on every site profile. The sitemap uses the owner's validated `enabledLanguages` for both marketing/collection URLs and reciprocal `hreflang`. Its `x-default` uses the configured default when enabled, otherwise the first enabled language. Missing or invalid language settings fall back to both static FR/EN variants; optional pages still require confirmed availability. `/galleries` and every `/e/*` customer gallery URL are omitted regardless of status. Both paths stay in `assets.run_worker_first` so the SPA fallback cannot replace them with HTML. The customer gallery directory and pages use `noindex,nofollow`; public gallery direct links still provide social preview metadata. A D1 outage leaves the core bilingual marketing sitemap available without collection URLs or optional pages. This does not change the existing static bilingual documents or their client-side language enforcement.
+
+Collection share metadata keeps the server's cover during initial API loading or failure, then uses the public API's owner-resolved `coverSources` large variant for both Open Graph and Twitter. An empty cover falls back to the profile's published share route; internal navigation updates the cover and returning Home restores its image. The Organization entity keeps the profile share image independently of the collection cover. No private gallery media or hardcoded demonstration photo is used.
 
 Published collection documents use narrow Worker-first routes because their bilingual copy and cover are edited after build time. The Worker inserts collection-specific title, description, canonical, language alternates, and share tags into the static Portfolio shell. Unpublished or unknown slugs return 404; a D1 outage returns 503 instead of publishing an incorrect Home canonical. Localized Portfolio indexes and the rest of the marketing site remain static. Legacy unprefixed interior pages and collection URLs redirect to the configured default language, preserving query parameters. Customer `/e/*` share URLs stay unprefixed and unindexed.
 
